//api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5890854864/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5891896197","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122560#issuecomment-5891896197","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122560","id":5891896197,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABXy8zhQ","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-29T14:03:57Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T14:05:40Z","body":"> Technically I feel it shouldn't happen since it shouldn't be kicked out faster than it's moved in\r\n\r\nI am skeptical about this opinion. If the character is stationary and there are colliders on removable costume accessories (like backpack), for example, this glitch might always occur when the accessories become stationary after being enabled.\r\n\r\n> Do you mean a Collider (one of the child nodes) is selected? Selecting a joint of the skeleton makes less sense.\r\n\r\nYes, right.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5891896197/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5892878835","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122560#issuecomment-5892878835","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122560","id":5892878835,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABXz4x8w","user":{"login":"goatchurchprime","id":677254,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NzI1NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/677254?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime","html_url":"https://github.com/goatchurchprime","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-29T15:01:57Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T15:01:57Z","body":"This wasn't the glitch I thought it was going to be.\r\n\r\nIt was caused by my assumption that the radius varies continuously rather than starts with a sharp edge partway along the chain.  I've fixed it by not discarding collisions before the start of the cone (which I has assumed would be hit by sphere end of the previous segment) and at the minimum colliding it at the `lamconemin` position, which is why it pushes slightly into the taper at the start.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"387\" height=\"570\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/be45c181-753b-4349-a498-12e31c1fb633\" />\r\n \r\nSorting out the gizmo highlighting is going to be a lot harder to do in a hurry because I've no idea where to start with regards to making it plot context-sensitive-wise on a node selection.\r\n\r\nLikewise, the other stuff is outside my area of competence to do properly without very specific instructions.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5892878835/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5893571903","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122560#issuecomment-5893571903","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122560","id":5893571903,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABX0jFPw","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-29T15:42:22Z","updated_at":"2026-09-29T15:42:22Z","body":"I have confirmed that it is stable with the cylinder shape now. However, for smoother colliding, meaning to allow a tapered capsule instead of a cylinder shape at the root, should we make it possible to set an arbitrary radius at the root? Just like the radius of the end_joint only works when extends_end_bone is enabled, we might be able to place a sphere that only works when chain collision is enabled.\r\n\r\nThough the sphere as a gizmo would likely be displayed under the same conditions as chain collision. Regarding the control of gizmo visibility, I think I can help adjust it and provide a patch.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5893571903/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5906482536","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122560#issuecomment-5906482536","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122560","id":5906482536,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABYA3FaA","user":{"login":"goatchurchprime","id":677254,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3NzI1NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/677254?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime","html_url":"https://github.com/goatchurchprime","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/goatchurchprime/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-30T07:37:23Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T07:37:23Z","body":"Adding a radius onto the root would work, but it's more changes to the UI.  The root doesn't move, so this only effects that cone section.  I think you're also suggesting a feature of zero radius setting, which only makes sense for chains.  It won't be hard to debug, but it is a new thing to worry about for all the other cases.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5906482536/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]